      "text": "RESEARCH_NEEDS:\nHow to build strict typographic/information hierarchy so price is the dominant, immediately-legible element without decorative noise.\nHow to signal \"serious infrastructure\" rather than \"discount promotion\" through pricing framing and visual restraint (India-specific pricing psychology).\nHow to encode festive/cultural signal legibly and briefly without literal festive clipart, consistent with how Indian visual communication compresses culture into minimal cues.\n\nFINAL_PRODUCTION_PACKAGE\n\nDELIVERABLE\nOne static 4:5 poster, master file 2400\u00d73000 px (scalable to 1080\u00d71350 for social), RGB, print-safe margins. Single image, single concept, no variants.\n\nOBJECTIVE_INTERPRETATION\nThe customer needs a festive-season acquisition poster for an API product whose entire commercial hook is two prices (\u20b99 image / \u20b999 video). The stated risk is that low, round rupee numbers read as \"discount flyer\" unless the design frames them as engineered, infrastructure-grade pricing. Because aight's own site voice is plain, declarative, and proof-of-seriousness driven (prepaid rupees, one GST invoice, a founder who answers), the poster's credibility must come from the same register: precision, restraint, and a rate-card logic \u2014 not festive clipart or retail sale mechanics. Typography and hierarchy must therefore carry both the emotional (festive, premium) and functional (price, comprehension) load, since no product photography exists to lean on.\n\nCORE_CREATIVE_IDEA\n\"The Festive Rate Card.\" The poster is composed like a utility/telecom tariff card or a GST invoice header \u2014 a format Indian businesses already read as official, exact, and non-negotiable \u2014 rather than like a sale flyer. Two prices sit in a tabular, equal-weight rate table. Festivity is carried by a single restrained device (a hairline gold rangoli-lattice border and a warm lamp-glow gradient), never by literal diyas, fireworks, or \"OFFER/SALE\" iconography. The pitch to the viewer is implicit: this isn't a discount, it's what the infrastructure actually costs \u2014 echoing the site's own framing of pricing as structural (prepaid, capped, invoiced) rather than promotional.\n\nMESSAGE_AND_INFORMATION_HIERARCHY\n1. Price pair (\u20b99 / \u20b999, tabular, largest type on the page) \u2014 the single thing every viewer must retain, legible even at thumbnail size, no cultural code required to parse it (numerals travel universally).\n2. Unit labels (\"IMAGE GENERATION\" / \"VIDEO GENERATION\") \u2014 disambiguate the two prices instantly.\n3. Trust line (\"Prepaid rupees. One GST invoice. No surprise bills.\") \u2014 converts low price into infrastructure credibility, sourced verbatim in spirit from the site's own proof points.\n4. Wordmark + tagline (\"aight. \u2014 Where Indian businesses buy AI\") \u2014 brand anchor, deliberately modest in size relative to the price.\n5. Festive frame line (\"Festive-season infrastructure pricing\") \u2014 supplies seasonal context without discount language.\n6. CTA (\"Talk to us \u2014 getaight.ai\") + fine-print rate disclaimer \u2014 lowest priority, smallest type.\nEverything below tier 1 is optional to a skimming viewer; nothing above tier 1 is allowed to compete with it in size or contrast.\n\nVISUAL_SYSTEM\nPalette: near-black charcoal background, off-white type, single antique/brass-gold accent. No red/yellow \"sale\" colors, no multicolor festive gradient.\nGrid: strict single-column vertical grid, generous margins, center third reserved for the price block, top for wordmark, bottom for CTA/legal \u2014 structure emerges from grouping like-with-like information (price data together, trust data together, brand data together), so the layout reads as inevitable rather than decorated.\nTypography: one grotesk/neo-grotesque sans family across the whole poster, varying only weight and size; tabular (lining) figures mandatory so \u20b99 and \u20b999 share a baseline grid like a real rate card; small caps + letterspacing for labels to reinforce \"spec sheet\" tone.\nMotif: a single 1\u20132pt hairline border built from a repeating rangoli-derived diamond/dot lattice, running the full frame edge \u2014 geometric and architectural, not ornamental, so it reads as festive to an Indian viewer while still looking engineered. A soft warm glow in the upper third evokes lamplight without depicting a lamp.\nNo product photography, no people, no icons of AI (no robots/circuits), since the product is invisible infrastructure \u2014 the type system itself must do all persuasive work.\n\nPRODUCTION_RECIPE\n1. Generate the text-free background/texture/motif layer (prompt below).\n2. Set all copy and numerals as vector type in a design tool on the grid specified above (deterministic, not generated).\n3. Composite type over background; apply the gold hairline divider between the two price rows.\n4. QA pass at three sizes: full res, 1080px feed, 300px thumbnail \u2014 confirm \u20b99 and \u20b999 remain instantly legible and correctly rendered at all three.\n5. Final color-grade/contrast check (off-white text \u2265 4.5:1 contrast against charcoal); export 4:5 master and social crop.\n\nGENERATION_PROMPTS\nSingle base-layer generation prompt (background only \u2014 all text added deterministically afterward):\n\n\"A premium, minimal 4:5 vertical poster background for a serious AI infrastructure brand during India's festive season. Near-black charcoal background (#0B0B0C) with a soft, subtle warm dark-amber glow rising from the upper third, evoking diya lamplight without depicting any lamp, flame, or festive object literally. A thin (1\u20132pt) hairline geometric border in muted antique gold runs along all four edges, built from a small repeating rangoli-derived diamond-and-dot lattice \u2014 precise, symmetrical, architectural, not decorative or cartoonish. The central two-thirds of the frame must remain completely empty, clean, evenly lit, and free of any text, numerals, logos, people, product imagery, icons, fireworks, confetti, or clipart \u2014 this space is reserved for typography added later. Subtle fine grain / brushed-material micro-texture for tactile quality. Palette strictly limited to charcoal black, off-white, and one antique gold. No gradients beyond a faint soft glow, no lens flare, no bright multicolor festive elements. Mood: an engineering rate card crossed with a quiet festive invitation \u2014 expensive, restrained, confident. Output 2400\u00d73000 px, 4:5 aspect ratio, no watermark.\"\n\nConstruction plan for the type layer (deterministic, composited on top \u2014 see below).\n\nDETERMINISTIC_OR_NON_GENERATIVE_ELEMENTS\nAll text is deterministic vector type, never generated as pixels, because price accuracy is a hard constraint and generative text rendering of currency symbols/numerals is unreliable at this stakes level:\n- Wordmark: \"aight.\" \u2014 off-white, modest size, top-left.\n- Tagline: \"Where Indian businesses buy AI\" \u2014 Light weight, 60% opacity, beneath wordmark.\n- Price row 1: label \"IMAGE GENERATION\" (small caps, gold, letterspaced) + numeral \"\u20b99\" (Bold/Black, off-white, tabular figures, largest element on page) + suffix \"/ generation\" (Light, 70% opacity).\n- Gold hairline divider rule (same gold as border motif) between the two price rows.\n- Price row 2: label \"VIDEO GENERATION\" + numeral \"\u20b999\", identical size/weight/treatment to row 1 so both prices carry equal visual authority.\n- Trust line: \"Prepaid rupees. One GST invoice. No surprise bills.\" \u2014 off-white, medium weight, centered.\n- Festive frame line: \"Festive-season infrastructure pricing\" \u2014 small, gold, no \"SALE/OFFER/DISCOUNT/% OFF\" wording anywhere on the poster.\n- CTA: \"Talk to us \u2014 getaight.ai\" inside a slim outlined pill, off-white.\n- Fine print, bottom corner, low opacity: \"Introductory festive-season rate. Terms at getaight.ai.\"\nAll grid positions, type sizes, tracking values, and color hex codes are locked in production spec before compositing \u2014 no randomness permitted in this layer.\n\nAUDIO_AND_EDIT\nNot applicable. This is a single static image deliverable; no audio track or edit timeline is required.\n\nFAILURE_PREVENTION\n- Currency/numeral misrendering \u2192 mitigated entirely by rendering \u20b99/\u20b999 as deterministic vector type, never generated text.\n- Drifting into \"discount flyer\" territory \u2192 banned assets: starbursts, ribbons, \"%\", red/yellow sale colors, countdown/urgency language; enforced by rate-card tabular layout instead.\n- Festive motif turning kitsch/stock \u2192 motif restricted to one abstract geometric lattice + one glow, no literal diya/firework/confetti imagery, per construction plan.\n- Hierarchy collapse from clutter \u2192 hard cap of six copy blocks total; if any block competes visually with the price numerals in size or saturation, it is downsized in QA.\n- Illegibility at small/thumbnail sizes \u2192 mandatory three-size QA pass before export; tabular lining figures and sufficient weight chosen specifically for compression survival.\n- Overclaiming/legal exposure on \"festive rate\" \u2192 fine-print disclaimer included by default.\n\nHARD_CONSTRAINT_CHECK\n- Exactly one 4:5 poster produced: yes.\n- \u20b99 (image) and \u20b999 (video) both present and immediately understandable: yes \u2014 largest, tabular, equal-weight, deterministic type.\n- Feels like serious AI infrastructure company, not discount retail: yes \u2014 rate-card structure, restrained palette, no sale iconography, trust line drawn from the brand's actual infra proof points.\n- Typography and information hierarchy do most of the work: yes \u2014 no product photography or illustrative scene; the entire poster is type + one abstract motif.\n- Only getaight.ai used for brand/product facts: yes \u2014 wordmark, tagline, prepaid-rupee/GST/founder-support claims sourced only from the site snapshot; no other brand assumptions invented.\n- No image/video model or provider named or recommended: yes.\n- Single concept, no alternatives offered: yes.\n\nKNOWLEDGE_AND_WEBSITE_USE\nWebsite: https://getaight.ai (frozen snapshot) \u2014 used for wordmark form (\"Aight .\"), brand line (\"Where Indian businesses buy AI\"), and the three trust facts placed in the poster's reassurance line (prepaid rupee wallet, one domestic GST invoice, hands-on/founder support), and to confirm the brand's plain, declarative verbal register that the visual system was designed to match.\nCanon (ACCEPTED only):\n- sk_sam_c003_0003 (Samara, Making and Breaking the Grid) \u2014 structure/hierarchy should be read off content grouping, not imposed decoratively; grounded the single-column grid and the decision to group price data, trust data, and brand data into distinct, alignment-defined zones.\n- sk_rbwl_0080 (Bijapurkar, We Are Like That Only) \u2014 the \"supplier up-traded, not consumer down-traded\" reframing; grounded the core creative decision to present \u20b99/\u20b999 as engineered infrastructure pricing (rate-card framing) rather than as a discount, avoiding the \"cheap = downmarket\" trap.\n- t_dpci_0009 / scs_dpci_001 (Dwyer & Patel, Cinema India) \u2014 \"hierarchy of responses\": some elements read universally, others require a shared cultural code. Used to justify keeping the numerals as the universally legible top tier while reserving the gold/rangoli-lattice motif as a secondary, culturally-coded layer that need not be understood for the poster to function.",
